Task 01 — Part of #1202 (bash safety, the owner's step 1).
• Add tree-sitter-bash, the parser the owner named and the one Codex, Claude Code and opencode use. If it won't build here, switch to the pure-Rust brush-parser and say why on the ticket.
• A new src/bash_parse.rs pulls out every simple command in the parsed tree, including ones inside $( ), backticks, subshells and double quotes. analyze_bash_command then runs the existing safety checks on each one.
• The raw-text checks stay in place as a second net.
• When the parser fails, behaviour stays as it is today. Sending parse failures to confirmation is named as the next slice.
• Binary size, startup time and the crate choice go on #1202 before any code is edited.
• The list of known misses (18 of 33 checks) should shrink as these shapes start being refused; that test is built to fail until the list is updated.
• #1196 (echo "kill -9 1 at $(date)" refused) will not be fixed by this slice, because the raw-text check that causes it still runs. The task says so.

